---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: sites.groups
  size: 1
  alias: group
permalink: "/group/{{ group.id }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ group.name }}"
---

{% from "statbar.njk" import statbar %}
{% from "stacks.njk" import technology %}

<header class="detail-head">
	{#
		The heading and the way in, on one row. Right-aligned rather than under
		the description, because it is the one thing on this page a reader might
		have come to *do* — everything else here is something to read.
	#}
	<div class="group-title">
		{#
			The category's health beside its name: the share of its measured sites
			showing no red ring, which is the same question the leaderboard's first
			step asks of a single site.

			A proportion, so a curated dozen and a community list of a thousand are
			judged on the same terms — a category cannot look healthy by being small.
		#}
		<h2 class="page-hed">{{ group.name }}{% if group.health %}<span class="health-pill health-{{ group.health.band }}" title="{{ group.health.clean | num }} of {{ group.health.measured | num }} measured {{ group.health.measured | plural('site') }} in {{ group.name }} show no red ring ({{ group.health.pct }}%). Good is 50% or more, Warn 28% or more.">{{ "Good" if group.health.band == "good" else ("Warn" if group.health.band == "average" else "Bad") }}</span>{% endif %}</h2>
		{% if group.submitUrl %}
		<a class="cta" href="{{ group.submitUrl }}">{{ group.submitLabel }}</a>
		{% endif %}
	</div>
	{#
		`safe` because a description may carry a link — the community list names
		the repository it comes from, and that is worth being clickable. These
		strings are ours, written in config/sites.js, not anything a measured site
		supplies.
	#}
	{% if group.description %}<p class="lede">{{ group.description | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
	{#
		Coverage, then cadence. Measurement is rolling and invisible from the
		page, so "1,143 of 1,235 measured" reads as a gap to be closed rather than
		as a schedule doing its job — the second half says which it is.
	#}
	<p class="muted">
		{{ group.measured | num }} of {{ group.entries.length | countOf("site") }} measured
		{%- if group.freshnessHours %} · each site {{ group.freshnessHours | cadence }}
		{%- if group.lastMeasured %}, most recently <time datetime="{{ group.lastMeasured | iso }}">{{ group.lastMeasured | since }}</time> ago{% endif %}
		{%- endif %}
	</p>
	{#
		The other half of the note on the home page's Perfect scores board. Said
		here too because this is where someone notices the absence: a starter with
		full marks that is not on that board looks like an oversight unless the
		page it *is* on explains itself.

		Read from the category rather than counted from its rows, so it still says
		so before anything here has been measured.
	#}
	{% if group.excludeFromPerfectScores %}
	<p class="muted small">
		Perfect scores here are kept off the <a href="/#leaderboard">home page's board</a>.
		These are demonstrations of a stack rather than sites someone runs, so full
		marks is the expected result. They rank normally on this page and in the
		overall leaderboard.
	</p>
	{% endif %}
</header>

{# The same tiles as the home page, over this category alone. #}
{% if group.stats.measured %}{{ statbar(group.stats, metrics) }}{% endif %}

{% if not group.entries.length %}
<div class="empty"><p>No sites in this group.</p></div>
{% else %}

{#
	Computed before the section so the section itself can be skipped. An empty
	"Biggest movers" heading followed by an apology is worse than no heading:
	most groups have nothing significant to report most of the time, and a
	permanent empty panel trains you to scroll past it.
#}
{#
	The four sites whose performance score moved furthest since the run before,
	in either direction. Chosen and ordered in lib/report.js — by absolute change,
	which a template cannot sort on.
#}
{% if group.topMovers.length %}
<section class="panel">
	<h2>Biggest movers</h2>
	<p class="muted small">
		Sites whose performance score moved more than this group's normal
		run-to-run noise. Everything else is jitter and is deliberately hidden.
	</p>
	<ul class="mover-cards">
		{% for m in group.topMovers %}
		<li class="mover-card {{ m.vsPrevious | deltaClass }}">
			<a class="site-link" href="/site/{{ m.slug }}/">
				{% set avatar = m.url | avatar(meta.avatarService) %}
				{% if avatar %}<img class="favicon" src="{{ avatar }}" width="32" height="32" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}
				<span title="{{ m.displayUrl }}">{{ m.displayUrl }}</span>
			</a>
			<span class="mover-delta">{{ m.vsPrevious | deltaArrow }} {{ m.vsPrevious | deltaText }}</span>
			<span class="mover-scores">{{ m.previous }} &rarr; {{ m.current }}</span>
		</li>
		{% endfor %}
	</ul>
</section>
{% endif %}

{#
	Past this many entries the table stops being something you read and becomes
	something you scroll past, so a large category shows only its clean rows and
	names the rest underneath. The threshold is on entries rather than measured
	sites: what makes the page unreadable is its length, and an unmeasured row
	takes up just as much of it.

	A presentation choice and nothing more — every stat on this page, the ranks
	in the table and the numbers in the bar above are all computed over the whole
	category. Nothing here filters what is counted.
#}
{% set MAX_FULL_ROWS = 500 %}
{% set filtered = group.entries.length > MAX_FULL_ROWS %}

{#
	An unranked category is listed alphabetically. Leaving it in score order would
	still read as a ranking — the order is the claim, whether or not it is
	numbered — and alphabetical says outright that the order carries no meaning
	while staying somewhere you can look a site up.
#}
{% set source = group.entries if group.ranked else group.entries | sortBy("displayUrl") %}

{% set rows = [] %}
{% set rest = [] %}
{#
	Clean rows only. A site with no figures — never measured, or failing every
	attempt — has nothing to put in eleven columns, and a run of rows reading "not
	measured yet" is a worse answer than a name in the list below, which at least
	does not promise a table's worth of data. The list marks both cases with an
	icon.
#}
{% for entry in source %}
	{% if not filtered or entry.allGreen %}
		{% set rows = (rows.push(entry), rows) %}
	{% else %}
		{% set rest = (rest.push(entry), rest) %}
	{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<section class="panel">
	<h2>{{ "Leaderboard" if group.ranked else "Sites" }}</h2>
	{% if filtered %}
	<p class="muted small">
		Of {{ group.entries.length | num }} sites, showing the {{ rows.length | num }} with “good” scores (all green circles): every Lighthouse category at 90 or above, no axe violations, no Core Web Vital failing. The other {{ rest.length | num }} are in an overflow list below.
	</p>
	{% endif %}
	{% if not group.ranked %}
	<p class="muted small">
		Not ranked, listed alphabetically. Still measured in case they return!
	</p>
	{% else %}
	<p class="muted small">
		Ranked by the circle color first: all green beats a row with amber, which beats red. Sites are not penalized for unknown Core Web Vitals. Tiebreakers include: sum of all four Lighthouse categories, fewest failing Core Web Vitals, then fewest axe violations, then Speed Index per KB — a heavy site outranks an empty one.
	</p>
	{% endif %}
	<div class="table-scroll">
	<table class="grid">
		<thead>
			<tr>
				{% if group.ranked %}<th class="col-rank">#</th>{% endif %}
				<th class="col-site">Site</th>
				<th class="col-stack" title="What built the site, detected from its generator tag or presumed from the list it is on">Tool</th>
				<th class="col-stack" title="Who serves the site, detected from its response headers on the same page load">Host</th>
				<th class="col-rings" title="The four Lighthouse categories, then violating nodes from a full axe run and the Core Web Vitals verdict from real users. The ranking breaks ties the other way round: Core Web Vitals first, then axe">Scores</th>
				<th class="col-trend">Perf trend</th>
				<th class="col-lcp"><span class="lcp-head">LCP</span></th>
				<th>CLS</th><th>TBT</th>
				<th title="Total bytes transferred, with the page's DOM element count beneath it. Element count is only shown where the DOM snapshot looked like a page that actually loaded">Weight</th><th>Req</th>
				<th class="col-lvf" title="The lab LCP as a multiple of the real-user p75. Above 1x the lab is slower than reality; below 1x the lab number is flattering the site. Only where CrUX has field data">Lab vs field</th>
				<th class="col-nojs" title="Share of pixels that differ between the page as rendered and the same page with scripts disabled. A shifted layout counts, so a noscript banner alone can account for a large figure. A warning mark means the page drew nothing at all without JavaScript. Only measured where a no-JS capture is stored">No-JS ∆</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
		{% for entry in rows %}
			<tr{% if entry.currentlyFailing %} class="row-failing"{% endif %}>
				{% if group.ranked %}
				<td class="col-rank">
					{% if entry.groupRanks[group.id].overall %}
					<span class="trophy">{{ entry.groupRanks[group.id].overall | trophy }}</span><span class="hash">#</span>{{ entry.groupRanks[group.id].overall }}{% if entry.groupRanks[group.id].overallClimb %}<span class="rank-climb" title="Up {{ entry.groupRanks[group.id].overallClimb }} {{ "place" if entry.groupRanks[group.id].overallClimb == 1 else "places" }} in this category since the previous measurement, from #{{ entry.groupRanks[group.id].overallPrevious }}">&#9650;{{ entry.groupRanks[group.id].overallClimb }}</span>{% endif %}
					{% else %}—{% endif %}
				</td>
				{% endif %}
				<td class="col-site">
					<a class="site-link" href="/site/{{ entry.slug }}/">
						{% set avatar = entry.url | avatar(meta.avatarService) %}
						{% if avatar %}<img class="favicon" src="{{ avatar }}" width="32" height="32" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}
						<span title="{{ entry.displayUrl }}">{{ entry.displayUrl }}</span>
					</a>
					{% if entry.latest %}<span class="updated-tag {{ 'stale-age' if entry.dataStale }}" title="Measured {{ entry.latest.date | date('long') }}"><time datetime="{{ entry.latest.date | iso }}">{{ entry.latest.date | since }}</time></span>{% else %}<span class="updated-tag never">never</span>{% endif %}
					{% if entry.currentlyFailing %}<span class="badge badge-error" title="{{ entry.lastError }}">failing</span>{% endif %}
					{% if entry.redirectTo and entry.redirectTo != entry.url %}<span class="badge badge-redirect" title="Measured through a redirect to {{ entry.redirectTo }}{% if entry.redirectConfirmed %} — confirmed, so history will follow it{% else %} — {{ entry.redirectReason }}{% endif %}">&#8618; redirect</span>
					{% elif entry.canonicalUrl %}<span class="badge badge-redirect" title="Measured through a redirect to {{ entry.canonicalUrl }} — the site's canonical form of this URL">&#8618; redirect</span>{% endif %}
					{% if entry.unlisted %}<span class="badge badge-unlisted" title="Built with {{ entry.unlisted.generator }} but not in {{ entry.unlisted.groupName }} — nobody has submitted it to the 11ty/11ty-community repository">unlisted</span>{% endif %}
				</td>
				{% if entry.latest %}
					{# 22 rather than the shortcode's 16: these are the row's only
					   pictures, in a column of their own, and at 16 they read as
					   punctuation beside the numbers. The inline uses elsewhere — a
					   tally row, a stat, a heading — sit next to text and keep the
					   default. #}
					<td class="col-stack">
						{% if entry.generator %}{% stackIcon entry.generator, 22 %}
						{% elif entry.presumedGenerator %}{% stackIcon entry.presumedGenerator, 22 %}
						{% else %}<span class="stack-none" title="No generator detected">·</span>{% endif %}
					</td>
					<td class="col-stack">
						{% if entry.host %}{% stackIcon entry.host, 22 %}{% else %}<span class="stack-none" title="No host detected">·</span>{% endif %}
					</td>
					{#
						Six rings, in the order <speedlify2-score> draws them: the four
						Lighthouse categories, then Core Web Vitals and axe — the ranking's
						two tiebreakers in the order it applies them, and the two things
						Lighthouse's own categories do not cover. One column rather than
						three, so a row reads as one picture and matches the embeddable
						badge exactly.
					#}
					<td class="col-rings">
						<span class="rings">
						{% for score in metrics.SCORES %}
							{% scoreRing entry.latest.lab.scores[score.key], score.label %}
						{% endfor %}
						{% axeRing entry.axe %}
						{% cwvRing entry.cwvFailures, entry.cwv.assessed, entry.cwvWorst %}
						</span>
					</td>
					<td class="col-trend">{% sparkline entry.trends.performance %}</td>
					<td class="num col-lcp"><span class="lcp-cell"><span class="lcp-value">{{ entry.latest.lab.timings.lcp | ms }}</span>{% lcpBar entry.latest.lab.lcpBreakdown, entry.latest.lab.timings.lcp %}</span></td>
					<td class="num">{{ entry.latest.lab.timings.cls | unit("") }}</td>
					<td class="num">{{ entry.latest.lab.timings.tbt | ms }}</td>
					<td class="num">{% set domCount = entry.latest.lab.dom.elements %}{{ entry.latest.lab.weight.total | bytes }}{% if domCount %}<span class="weight-dom" title="{{ domCount | num }} DOM elements">{{ domCount | num }} elements</span>{% endif %}</td>
					<td class="num">{{ entry.latest.lab.weight.requests | num }}</td>
					<td class="num">{% if entry.labVsField %}<span class="lvf" title="Lab LCP {{ entry.labVsField.lab | ms }}, field p75 {{ entry.labVsField.field | ms }}">{{ entry.labVsField.ratio }}&times;</span>{% else %}<span class="muted">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
					<td class="num col-nojs">{% if entry.ownScreenshot and entry.ownScreenshot.difference !== null %}{{ entry.ownScreenshot.difference }}%{% if entry.clientRendered %}<span class="csr-yes" title="only {{ entry.ownScreenshot.noJsText }}% of the no-JS capture is text, so the page said nothing without its scripts"><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation csr-icon" width="12" height="12" aria-hidden="true"></i>EMPTY</span>{% endif %}{% else %}<span class="muted">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
				{% else %}
					{# 11 either way: dropping the rank column removes a cell from this row too,
   so the span covers the same remainder. #}
				<td colspan="11" class="muted">not measured yet</td>
				{% endif %}
			</tr>
		{% endfor %}
		</tbody>
	</table>
	</div>

	{#
		Right after the ranked table, for a reader who has finished the leaderboard
		itself — but only when there is an overflow list below to separate it from
		the one at the end of the page. Without that list the two would sit a
		paragraph apart, which reads as a stutter rather than as two exits.
	#}
	{% if group.submitUrl and rest.length %}
	<p class="cta-footer">
		<a class="cta" href="{{ group.submitUrl }}">{{ group.submitLabel }}</a>
	</p>
	{% endif %}

	{% if rest.length %}
	{#
		Names, not numbers. These rows were left out because the table was too long
		to read, so repeating the columns here would undo the point — the link is
		what is useful, and every figure is on the page it goes to.
	#}
	<h3 class="rest-head">
		The other {{ rest.length | num }}
		<span class="muted small">— at least one ring amber, red or unmeasured, in no particular order</span>
	</h3>
	{#
		Shuffled, and reshuffled on every build. There is no ranking left to show
		here — that is what the table above is for — so any fixed order would be
		read as one anyway, and alphabetical would put the same sites at the top
		of a 900-name list for ever.
	#}
	<ul class="rest-list">
		{% for entry in rest | shuffle %}
		<li>
			<a href="/site/{{ entry.slug }}/">{{ entry.displayUrl }}</a>
			{#
				The one thing worth saying here beyond the name: this row is not in
				the table because the site is down, rather than because its scores
				are middling. The title carries the error itself.
			#}
			{#
				Two independent marks, because they answer different questions and a
				site can need both. The hourglass says there are no figures on the
				page this links to; the triangle says the last attempt errored, and
				carries the error itself. Most of the sites with no figures have both
				— nothing to show, and a reason why — but each stands alone: a site
				measured months ago can be failing today, and a site added this
				morning has neither been tried nor refused.

				The hourglass first: what is missing, then why. Muted rather than red,
				since a site nobody has measured yet is a gap in our data and not a
				verdict on theirs.
			#}
			{%- if not entry.latest %}
			<i class="fa-solid fa-hourglass-start rest-pending" title="No successful measurement yet" width="12" height="12">No results yet</i>
			{%- endif %}
			{%- if entry.currentlyFailing %}
			<i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation rest-error" title="{{ entry.lastError }}" width="12" height="12">Currently failing</i>
			{%- endif %}
		</li>
		{% endfor %}
	</ul>
	{% endif %}

	{#
		Last on the page, after the overflow list as well as the table. Someone who
		has read both and still not found their own site is exactly who this is
		for, and by then the header is a thousand rows away.
	#}
	{% if group.submitUrl %}
	<p class="cta-footer">
		<a class="cta" href="{{ group.submitUrl }}">{{ group.submitLabel }}</a>
	</p>
	{% endif %}
</section>

{#
	After the leaderboard, matching the home page's order: the tables are what
	someone came for, and this is the summary you read once you have looked. Over
	this category's sites alone, so it answers what a category is usually for —
	what these particular sites have in common.
#}
{{ technology(group.stacks, "stacks") }}
{% endif %}
